      "description": "`len` is computed from `strlen(s) + 1` before it is used as a size/length argument; wraparound can shrink the allocation or copy bound.",
      "root_cause": "Size arithmetic is performed before proving operands are bounded.",
      "suggested_fix": "Check operands before the arithmetic, or use a checked size helper.",
      "confidence": 0.82,
      "impact_level": "medium",
      "reasoning": "确定性规则 `arithmetic_size_before_sink` 在 `_str_dup` 的 `src/utils.c:42` 命中了 `integer_overflow`（CWE-190） 候选。\n问题判断：`len` is computed from `strlen(s) + 1` before it is used as a size/length argument; wraparound can shrink the allocation or copy bound.\n数据/资源路径：源/对象 `strlen(s) + 1` -> 汇点/操作 `len used by allocation/copy`。\n保护状态：当前函数内未看到足够的边界检查、所有权转移或同步保护。\n关键证据：\n- line 42: arithmetic size expression `strlen(s) + 1`\n- nearby allocation/copy consumes the computed size\n反向证据：未发现能否定该候选的本地保护或清理证据。\n根因：Size arithmetic is performed before proving operands are bounded.\n建议：Check operands before the arithmetic, or use a checked size helper.",
